      "writtenOn": "2022-11-02T08:56:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah, especially since StructsInFunctions did not change at all but I\u0027m guessing the program looks different when run as a RTE. The SPIR-V validation error looks like:\n```\nSPIR-V validation error: CompositeConstruct must appear in a block\n  %126 \u003d OpCompositeConstruct %S_S1_c0 %float_2 %int_3\n\n```\n\nI wonder if this is because I passed `fConstantBuffer` instead `out` to writeExpression, as you also noted. I\u0027m surprised that didn\u0027t actually make a difference in the golden file but it looks like it\u0027s the wrong thing to do regardless. Giving it a try now.",
