      "writtenOn": "2022-11-02T12:50:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Oh, thanks for the extra info. Now this makes sense actually. \"OpCompositeConstruct float 2, int 3\" is the result from `constructs_a_struct`. Writing a struct goes through `writeCompositeConstructor` -\u003e `writeOpCompositeConstruct`. `writeOpCompositeConstruct` is smart enough to OpConstant-ify vectors and matrices, but for structs there is no smart handling at all and it always uses OpCompositeConstruct. This is totally a \"not-according-to-plan\" path. Using `out` should have fixed it.",
      "parentUuid": "3d4835b7_5d79e2a6",
