      },
      "lineNbr": 3486,
      "author": {
        "id": 11059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-02T21:01:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`*varDecl.value()` is an Expression which might be a VariableReference. e.g.:\n\nvarDecl: `const float x \u003d PI;`\nvarDecl.value(): `VariableReference PI`\nGetConstantValueForVariable(*varDecl.value()): `Literal 3.14`\nAnalysis::IsCompileTimeConstant(Literal 3.14): `true`\n\nOr:\n\nvarDecl: `float y \u003d Foo();`\nvarDecl.value(): `FunctionCall Foo()`\nGetConstantValueForVariable(*varDecl.value()): `FunctionCall Foo()` (returned as-is)\nAnalysis::IsCompileTimeConstant(FunctionCall Foo()): `false`",
      "parentUuid": "1c6084d3_6def3762",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3485,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 3486,
        "endChar": 55
      },
      "revId": "aa64c693c4800db67205d3216d23c8fc5489b8be",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "92af9dcb_68f9999e",
        "filename": "src/sksl/codegen/SkSLSPIRVCodeGenerator.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 3486,
      "author": {
        "id": 18529
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-02T21:45:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thank you for the clarification, I think it\u0027s very helpful. This makes sense for the rhs of the initial value assignment, which may be a VariableReference but I think the code here still needs to check that the lhs (i.e. the declared variable) has a const modifier. Otherwise the code would eliminate declarations like `float x \u003d PI` which won\u0027t get OpConstant-ified in `writeWriteVariableReference` (as `GetConstantValueOrNullForVariable` will return nullptr for references to `x). Sure enough, I hit assertions on many non-const variables being missing in `fVariableMap` if I don\u0027t explicitly filter for `var-\u003emodifiers().fFlags \u0026 Modifiers::kConst_Flag` here.\n\nGiven that\u0027s necessary, it feels redundant to call `GetConstantValueForVariable` and also call `Analysis::IsCompileTimeConstant` on the initial value (which will also walk the entire expression tree).\n\nI may be missing the complete picture here but I think `GetConstantValueForVariable` would have to also work for a `VarDeclaration` and check the const modifiers for the lhs. I think that may remove the need to call `Analysis::IsCompileTimeConstant` on the initial value. Otherwise simply checking for `if (var-\u003emodifiers().fFlags \u0026 Modifiers::kConst_Flag \u0026\u0026 Analysis::IsCompileTimeConstant(*varDecl.value())) {` here has the same result and keeps the code clear.",
      "parentUuid": "cda84ba9_d314af91",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3485,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 3486,
        "endChar": 55
      },
      "revId": "aa64c693c4800db67205d3216d23c8fc5489b8be",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "748a4ba0_e23ed5d7",
        "filename": "src/sksl/codegen/SkSLSPIRVCodeGenerator.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 3486,
      "author": {
        "id": 11059
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-11-02T22:04:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You\u0027re right--checking for `const` on the decl flags is necessary--that makes sense. Thanks for clarifying this.\n\nBut `Analysis::IsCompileTimeConstant(*initialValue)` will return false for an initial-value expression of `VarDeclaration PI` so AFAICS this will generate an OpVariable for our `x` decl here, won\u0027t it? \n\nMaybe we don\u0027t actually have a test case that creates a `const` variable whose initial-value is just another `const` variable...? Just to be sure, please try creating a test like like this and check the output:\n\n```\n{\n  const float PI \u003d 3.14;\n  const float x \u003d PI;\n  // Use x in some code to prevent it from being eliminated\n}\n```\n\nUnless I\u0027m confused, this is where you will see the need for this call to `GetConstantValueForVariable`. If we don\u0027t have a test like this today, I think it\u0027s worth adding it.\n\nBTW, do not worry about \"walking the expression tree\" performance re `IsCompileTimeConstant` or `GetConstantValueForVariable`. Both of these calls early-out as soon as they find a mismatch, and the matching trees are just a leaf (Literal/VariableReference) or a 1-deep tree of 2-4 leaves (Constructor[2~4 Literals]). They are realistically a lot closer to O(1) than O(N).",
      "parentUuid": "92af9dcb_68f9999e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3485,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 3486,
        "endChar": 55
      },
      "revId": "aa64c693c4800db67205d3216d23c8fc5489b8be",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
