      "writtenOn": "2022-11-03T00:13:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Unfortunately I don\u0027t think your test is working as expected.\n\n`kFloatConstantAlias` is only used in a constant-foldable context (`1.0 + kFloatConstantAlias`). This binary expression will be folded into a Literal, and then `kFloatConstantAlias` will be eliminated because it has no references left.\n\n`kLocalFloatConstantAlias` is only used in a constant-foldable context (`half4(kLocalFloatConstantAlias)` will be folded into `half4(Literal)`) and then `kLocalFloatConstantAlias` will be eliminated because it has no references left.\n\nPlease use one of these variables in a way that we can\u0027t possibly fold it, e.g. `if (kFloatConstantAlias \u003d\u003d myUniform)`. If you put it into a foldable expression, it will get hit by the ConstantFolder bat and will likely be simplified out. Using a uniform (or even a non-constant variable!) is an easy way to prevent it from being folded.",
      "parentUuid": "febf7ecb_f3cae7d8",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3485,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 3486,
